\pard\sa240\qc\b\f0\fs32 SolarEdge Dashboard Solution Design\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\qc\f0 Version 1.0\par
\pard\sa240\qc\f0 Date: 2026-05-19\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 1. Document Purpose\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa140\f0 This document defines the implementation-oriented solution design for evolving the SolarEdge dashboard from direct upstream querying to a persisted data platform backed by a free online database. It complements the architecture specification and focuses on delivery, interfaces, schema, migration, and operational behavior.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 2. Scope\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 In scope:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Database-backed persistence for historical energy data.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Scheduled ingestion from SolarEdge.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. API changes to serve data from persistence.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Rollup generation for dashboard performance.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Operational monitoring and stale-data reporting.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 6. Migration path from current implementation.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Out of scope:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. User authentication and multi-tenant administration.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Native mobile applications.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Billing, monetization, or enterprise governance features.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 3. Business Goals\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Reduce page load dependency on SolarEdge availability.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Preserve historical energy data beyond transient API access.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Enable faster chart generation for large time ranges.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Improve operational resilience through retries, audit logs, and backfills.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Keep infrastructure cost at or near free-tier level.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 4. Recommended Target Stack\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Frontend: existing static dashboard with Chart.js.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Backend API: existing Node.js and Express service.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Database: Supabase PostgreSQL.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Scheduler: GitHub Actions cron, Supabase scheduled function, or a lightweight hosted cron job.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Secrets management: environment variables in backend and CI only.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 5. Solution Overview\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
+----------------+      +---------------------+      +------------------+\par
| SolarEdge API  | ---> | Ingestion Service   | ---> | Supabase DB      |\par
| energyDetails  |      | fetch + retry       |      | raw + rollups    |\par
| currentPower   |      | upsert + audit      |      | sync_runs        |\par
+----------------+      +----------+----------+      +--------+---------+\par
                                     |                          |\par
                                     |                          |\par
                                     v                          v\par
                           +---------------------+      +------------------+\par
                           | Aggregation Service | ---> | Express API      |\par
                           | query / rollups     |      | /api/energy      |\par
                           | fallback rules      |      | /api/power/live  |\par
                           +---------------------+      +--------+---------+\par
                                                                     |\par
                                                                     v\par
                                                           +------------------+\par
                                                           | Browser Dashboard|\par
                                                           | charts + filters |\par
                                                           +------------------+\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 6. Core Design Decisions\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Persist raw upstream samples before relying on pre-aggregated values.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Use idempotent upsert logic keyed by site, timestamp, and granularity.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Keep SolarEdge API access server-side only.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Query raw data for short intervals and rollups for long intervals.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Keep live power flow as a separate runtime endpoint.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 7. Logical Components and Responsibilities\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\b\f0 7.1 SolarEdge Client\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Responsibilities:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Call SolarEdge endpoints such as energyDetails and currentPowerFlow.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Handle retries and transient network failures.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Normalize upstream errors into application-level exceptions.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 7.2 Ingestion Service\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Responsibilities:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Determine time windows for fetch jobs.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Retrieve raw SolarEdge samples.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Upsert samples into the database.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Record sync run status and metrics.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 7.3 Aggregation Service\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Responsibilities:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Read raw samples and rollups.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Select the correct granularity based on the requested interval.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Compute KPI values for API responses.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Fall back to direct upstream reads only when necessary.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 7.4 Repository Layer\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Responsibilities:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Abstract data reads and writes from the rest of the application.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Encapsulate SQL or database client logic.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Support unit testing via repository stubs or mocks.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 7.5 API Layer\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Responsibilities:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Validate request parameters.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Request summary data from the aggregation service.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Return stable chart-ready JSON to the frontend.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Expose health and sync diagnostics.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 8. Proposed Database Schema\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\b\f0 Table: sites\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Purpose: store one or more SolarEdge site identities.\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
sites (\par
  id uuid primary key,\par
  external_site_id text not null unique,\par
  name text null,\par
  timezone text not null,\par
  created_at timestamptz not null default now()\par
)\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Table: energy_samples\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Purpose: store raw time-series values.\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
energy_samples (\par
  id uuid primary key,\par
  site_id uuid not null references sites(id),\par
  timestamp_utc timestamptz not null,\par
  granularity text not null,\par
  production_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  consumption_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  grid_import_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  grid_export_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  self_consumed_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  source text not null,\par
  created_at timestamptz not null default now(),\par
  unique(site_id, timestamp_utc, granularity)\par
)\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Table: energy_rollups_daily\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
energy_rollups_daily (\par
  id uuid primary key,\par
  site_id uuid not null references sites(id),\par
  day_utc date not null,\par
  production_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  consumption_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  grid_import_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  grid_export_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  self_consumed_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  updated_at timestamptz not null default now(),\par
  unique(site_id, day_utc)\par
)\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Table: energy_rollups_monthly\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
energy_rollups_monthly (\par
  id uuid primary key,\par
  site_id uuid not null references sites(id),\par
  month_utc date not null,\par
  production_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  consumption_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  grid_import_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  grid_export_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  self_consumed_wh numeric not null default 0,\par
  updated_at timestamptz not null default now(),\par
  unique(site_id, month_utc)\par
)\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Table: sync_runs\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
sync_runs (\par
  id uuid primary key,\par
  site_id uuid not null references sites(id),\par
  sync_type text not null,\par
  started_at timestamptz not null,\par
  finished_at timestamptz null,\par
  status text not null,\par
  records_written integer not null default 0,\par
  error_message text null\par
)\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 9. Data Retention and Query Strategy\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Retain all raw 15-minute samples for the full project lifetime if volume remains within free-tier limits.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Use raw samples for intraday views.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Use daily rollups for weekly and monthly views.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Use monthly rollups for yearly views.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Rebuild rollups from raw data when calculation logic changes.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 10. API Design Changes\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\b\f0 Existing endpoints to retain\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 GET /api/health\par
\pard\sa120\f0 GET /api/power/live\par
\pard\sa120\f0 GET /api/energy?start=YYYY-MM-DD&end=YYYY-MM-DD\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 New endpoints proposed\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 GET /api/sync/status\par
\pard\sa120\f0 POST /api/sync/run (protected, optional)\par
\pard\sa120\f0 GET /api/diagnostics/staleness (optional)\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 API response principle\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 The frontend should continue receiving chart-ready payloads. Internal storage details must remain hidden behind the API.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 11. Internal Interface Design\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f1\fs18
EnergyRepository\par
  - upsertSamples(samples)\par
  - getSamples(siteId, start, end, granularity)\par
  - getDailyRollups(siteId, start, end)\par
  - getMonthlyRollups(siteId, start, end)\par
  - saveSyncRun(syncRun)\par
  - updateSyncRun(syncRun)\par
\par
IngestionService\par
  - syncRecent(siteId)\par
  - syncRange(siteId, start, end, granularity)\par
  - backfillDay(siteId, day)\par
\par
AggregationService\par
  - getEnergySummary(siteId, start, end)\par
  - selectGranularity(start, end)\par
  - buildKpis(points)\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs22

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 12. Scheduling Design\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Recommended schedule:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Every 15 minutes: fetch current day intraday updates.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Every night: backfill the previous day in case SolarEdge publishes late corrections.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Every week: run a gap detection job and rebuild any missing ranges.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Suggested GitHub Actions model\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Workflow uses encrypted repository secrets.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Workflow runs a sync script.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Workflow writes audit result to sync_runs through the backend or direct DB client.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 13. Environment Configuration\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Required runtime configuration:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. SOLAREDGE_API_KEY\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. SOLAREDGE_SITE_ID\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. DATABASE_URL or Supabase connection settings\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Optional sync token for protected administrative endpoints\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 14. Implementation Phases\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\b\f0 Phase 1: Persistence Foundation\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Deliverables:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Add repository abstraction.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Introduce Supabase client configuration.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Create tables and indexes.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Exit criteria: database schema exists and repository integration tests pass.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Phase 2: Raw Ingestion\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Deliverables:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Implement sync command for a date range.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Implement idempotent upsert behavior.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Write sync_runs audit records.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Exit criteria: a day of data can be synced and re-synced without duplication.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Phase 3: Database-backed API\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Deliverables:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Change /api/energy to read from the database.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Preserve current API response shape for the frontend.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Add stale-data logic and fallback behavior if required.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Exit criteria: the UI functions without direct historical reads from SolarEdge.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Phase 4: Rollups and Performance\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Deliverables:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Daily rollup generation.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Monthly rollup generation.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Query planner logic for interval-based reads.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Exit criteria: long-range dashboard loads stay fast and stable.\par

\pard\sa120\b\f0 Phase 5: Operations and Monitoring\b0\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Deliverables:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Scheduled sync workflows.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Sync status endpoint or admin page.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Alerting or visible stale-data signal.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Exit criteria: operators can tell whether data is healthy and current.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 15. Risks and Mitigations\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Risk: SolarEdge throttling or intermittent network resets.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Mitigation: retry policy, backoff, scheduled backfill, and sync audit logs.\par

\pard\sa120\f0 Risk: free-tier database sleeping or quota constraints.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Mitigation: use rollups, limit excessive polling, and keep the API query pattern efficient.\par

\pard\sa120\f0 Risk: timestamp misalignment or timezone drift.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Mitigation: store UTC timestamps only and convert at presentation boundaries.\par

\pard\sa120\f0 Risk: inconsistent calculations after logic changes.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Mitigation: preserve raw samples and rebuild rollups deterministically.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 16. Testing Strategy\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Unit tests for repository query selection and KPI calculations.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Unit tests for idempotent upsert behavior.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Integration tests for syncing a known date range into the database.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. API regression tests preserving current response contracts.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Scheduled-job smoke tests in a non-production environment.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 17. Acceptance Criteria\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Historical chart requests are served from the database for normal operation.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Raw sync jobs can run repeatedly without duplicate records.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Daily and monthly chart ranges load within acceptable time on the free tier.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Sync status and failures are visible through logs or an API endpoint.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. The browser never receives the SolarEdge API key.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 18. Recommended First Sprint\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Sprint objective: create the persistence backbone without changing the frontend contract.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 Scope:\par
\pard\sa120\f0 1. Add repository abstraction.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 2. Create Supabase schema.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 3. Implement manual range sync command.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 4. Store one day of real data successfully.\par
\pard\sa120\f0 5. Read that same day through the API from the database.\par

\pard\sa220\b\f0\fs24 19. Final Design Recommendation\b0\fs22\par
\pard\sa140\f0 Implement the solution in phases, beginning with raw sample persistence and repository abstraction. Do not start with complex rollups or admin tooling before the database-backed ingestion path is stable. The preferred outcome is a Supabase-backed service that preserves raw SolarEdge data, serves chart-ready API responses efficiently, and supports reliable scheduled synchronization on a free tier.\par

\pard\sa200\qc\i\f0 End of solution design\i0\par
